@*
    The handoff's archetype 6, Admin edit (.design/handoff/PageAdminEdit.dc.html): a
    page head with crumbs and the Save action, then the form column, then the
    record's history.

    Unlike a detail page, the head is always drawn - "Edit module" is known before
    the module is - so loading and not-found replace only the body:

      loading     a LoadingBlock
      not found   NotFound: the record is gone, or never existed. No form, and no
                  history, because there is nothing to have a history of.
      editing     Notices, ChildContent, History

    The form itself stays with the page. `.edit-col` is usually the <form> element,
    and the @onsubmit belongs to whoever owns the model - so ChildContent is the
    page's own <form class="edit-col">, not something this component wraps.

    History is a slot, not a query. AuditHistoryPanel opens its own DbContext
    through the factory because it loads while the page around it may be saving
    (CLAUDE.md, #741); it must stay a sibling component, never a read folded into
    the page's context. The slot only decides where it goes and when it shows.

    A page with a sticky side panel (.gen__aside - the template editor's preview)
    puts its own layout in ChildContent; that is a body, not a frame.
*@

<div class="page@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(PageClass) ? "" : " " + PageClass)">
    <PageHead Title="@Title" Subtitle="@Subtitle" SubtitleContent="SubtitleContent"
              Trail="Trail" Crumbs="Crumbs" Actions="Actions" ShowActions="ShowActions" Sticky="Sticky" />

    @Notices

    @if (IsLoading)
    {
        <LoadingBlock Text="@LoadingText" />
    }
    else if (IsNotFound)
    {
        @NotFound
    }
    else
    {
        @ChildContent
        @History
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    [Parameter] public string Subtitle { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? SubtitleContent { get; set; }
    /// <summary>The breadcrumb steps, the page itself last and unlinked.</summary>
    [Parameter] public IReadOnlyList<Crumb>? Trail { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Crumbs { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Back, Save, and whatever else acts on the whole record.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Actions { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public bool ShowActions { get; set; } = true;

    /// <summary>Keep the head, and so Save, in view while a long form scrolls.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Sticky { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Alerts between the head and the form, in every state: save results, query-string outcomes.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Notices { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool IsLoading { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string LoadingText { get; set; } = "Loading...";

    [Parameter] public bool IsNotFound { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? NotFound { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The form - normally the page's own <c>&lt;form class="edit-col"&gt;</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The record's <c>AuditHistoryPanel</c>, under the form. Shown only while editing.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? History { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Extra class on the <c>.page</c> wrapper, for a page-scoped stylesheet to hang on.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? PageClass { get; set; }
}
